            <title>[LU-21010] tests: check_mem_leak does not detect LNet memory leaks</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21010</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Problem&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;On master, `check_mem_leak()` in `test-framework.sh` does not detect an LNet (Portals) memory leak. Tests that unload the modules pass even when LNet leaks memory.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Environment&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;master since &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18687" title="Separate userspace/compat code from kernel code" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18687"&gt;LU-18687&lt;/a&gt; "debug: cleanly split lustre_compat and debug" (commit 7fa1ec5446, landed 2026-02-10).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Any node. b_es7_0 is not affected.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Reproduction&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;1. Make LNet leak memory. The reproducer in &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21009" title="lnet: discovery completes a peer with a push in flight and leaks the peer" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21009"&gt;LU-21009&lt;/a&gt; is one way.&lt;br/&gt;
2. Unload the modules with `unload_modules_local` or `unload_modules`.&lt;br/&gt;
3. The console shows `(module.c:646:debug_module_exit()) Portals memory leaked: 320 bytes`. `check_mem_leak()` returns 0.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Analysis&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;`check_mem_leak()` matches the leak line with this pattern:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;dmesg | tail -n 20 | grep -E -i "libcfs.*memory leaked"
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18687" title="Separate userspace/compat code from kernel code" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18687"&gt;LU-18687&lt;/a&gt;, `libcfs_exit()` printed the message, so the line contained "libcfs". Now `debug_module_exit()` prints it, and the line does not contain "libcfs". The pattern matches nothing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;b_es7_0 still prints the message from `libcfs_exit()`, and its `check_mem_leak()` catches the same leak.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Proposed fix&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Match the message text instead of the function name, for example `grep -E "Portals memory leaked"`. This works for the old and the new function name.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
